  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "Deploy a7b8c9d renamed the invoices.amount column to amount_cents in a single step - the migration and the code change shipped together. During the rolling deploy, instances still on the old code queried invoices.amount, which no longer existed, so ~50% of invoice writes (the fraction on old instances) failed with 'column does not exist'. This is an expand/contract violation: the rename was not backwards-compatible with the in-flight old version. Errors cleared once every instance was on the new code.",
    "evidence_path": [
      "deploy a7b8c9d at 22:00 applies migration 20261117 renaming invoices.amount, rolling out",
      "billing-api ERROR: old instances hit 'column invoices.amount does not exist' (42703)",
      "~50% of invoice writes fail during the rollout, matching the old/new instance split",
      "schema_errors_per_s spikes then falls as the rollout completes",
      "errors clear once all 12 hosts are on the new code"
    ],
    "fix": "Complete the rollout to stop the bleeding (done). Split such changes: add amount_cents alongside amount, deploy code that writes both and reads the new one, backfill, then drop amount in a later release. Add a migration lint that blocks non-backwards-compatible renames.",
    "should_escalate": false
  }
}
